<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Focal epilepsy on levetiracetam (G40.109)</content>. Seizure-free for six and a half months; kidney function normal (creatinine 0.76 mg/dL, eGFR 95). PHQ-9 4; MoCA 29. [S]<list><item>Continue levetiracetam 500 mg twice a day.</item><item>At one year after surgery: EEG and a shared decision about tapering.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Meningioma, CNS WHO grade 1, after resection (D32.0)</content>. No symptoms of recurrence. [S]<list><item>MRI one year after surgery.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Viral gastroenteritis (A08.4)</content>. Resolved without complications or seizures. [S]<list><item>Keep the plan for vomited doses in her diary.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure diary, triggers (sleep loss, alcohol, missed doses), and seizure first aid</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No seizures in six and a half months; one vomited dose in August was managed by plan</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9, with a question about irritability on levetiracetam</td><td>Every visit while on levetiracetam and during cancer treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4, minimal; counseling completed</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GAD-7</td><td>Every visit during the diagnostic and treatment phase; then as needed</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Mild at the last visit and no anxiety reported now; to be repeated if symptoms return</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen after brain surgery</td><td>Baseline and after treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>MoCA 29, up from 27 before surgery</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Kidney function on levetiracetam</td><td>Baseline, then periodically, because the drug is cleared by the kidneys</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Creatinine 0.76 mg/dL; eGFR 95</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Surveillance MRI</td><td>Yearly for five years after the three-month scan</td><td>Due</td><td>One year after surgery</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>EEG before any taper</td><td>Before deciding to stop an antiseizure medicine</td><td>Due</td><td>At one year after surgery</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>A diagnosis within two weeks, explained in plain words with the images and reports. Outcome by 2026-03-17: MRI and EEG within a week; diagnosis explained at two weeks with the images [S]</item><item>No further seizures. In progress; target 2027-04-07 [S]</item><item>Full use of the right hand and return to writing every morning. Outcome by 2026-09-29: Grip equal on both sides by three months; writing every morning [S]</item><item>Decide on treatment herself after hearing the options, benefits, and harms. Outcome by 2026-03-17: Chose resection after observation and radiosurgery were explained [S]</item><item>Mood and grief supported: PHQ-9 below 5 and a counselor available. Outcome by 2026-09-29: PHQ-9 4 at six months; completed eight sessions with the neuro-oncology counselor [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: EANO guideline on the diagnosis and management of meningiomas. Goldbrunner R, et al. Neuro Oncol 2021;23(11):1821-1834 (2021); Evidence-based guideline: Management of an unprovoked first seizure in adults. Krumholz A, et al. Neurology 2015;84(16):1705-1713 (2015); SNO and EANO practice guideline update: Anticonvulsant prophylaxis in patients with newly diagnosed brain tumors. Walbert T, et al. Neuro Oncol 2021;23(11):1835-1844 (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (depression screening and PHQ-9 follow-up) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit next month; MRI and EEG at one year after surgery with a review of levetiracetam. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-20: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

